      "message": "I think we need a comment here to explain that on T-, data activity tracking was already removed by the updateDefaultNetwork call above..\n\nEven so, this is going to be pretty hard to follow. Would suggest refactoring to make it clearer. I think maybe we can move the LegacyNetworkActivityTracker out to its own file, and in ConnectivityService, instead of calling methods on it that leak implementation details (e.g., \"removeDataActivityTracking\"), we could call more generic methods such as \"notifyNetworkConnected\", \"notifyNetworkDisconnected\", \"notifyDefaultNetworkChanged\". That would remove some of these isAtLeastU checks in ConnectivityService.\n\nThese can go in a follow-up as well I think.",
